})
.catch(err => {
console.error(err);
});
return unansweredQuestions;
};
We simply output any errors to the console.
It is important to note that requests that contain HTTP error codes are not
handled by the catch method. HTTP errors must be handled in the first
then method by looking at the ok or status properties on the response
parameter.
